 All edits stay inside `plugin/plugins/game_agent_minecraft/`. Live behavior improvement is a separate observation from context transport correctness; offline tests cannot establish that the model will never repeat a historical explanation.
 
 ## Offline verification
 
 The new tests failed before the change because `lastCheck` was absent (including unknown permission). A richer fixture with two scoped receipts and login welcome data then reproduced a 421/400-token overflow. The renderer now reduces optional skill metadata and shortens its preamble under pressure, retaining both permission facts. Full plugin regression: 77 tests passed at 11:03 Asia/Shanghai. Artifacts: `protection-context-red-20261009.log`, `protection-context-budget-red-20261009.log`, and `protection-context-regression-20261009.log` in the trial directory.
+
+## Deployment verification, 11:06 Asia/Shanghai
+
+Work commit `3d9a151` is deployed as `2cc30b4`. Dispatch was temporarily gated through the existing config API; the pending task was confirmed finished before the plugin-only reload. Unattended mode was restored and verified true. The Minecraft connection and model were kept running. Subsequent plugin passive callbacks were accepted by Neko main.
+
+`D:/neko-mc-trial/protection-context-verified-20261009.json` records a fresh, live plugin observation with break preflight (-576,48,-461), `allow_likely/true/no_known_protection`, and no cached denial. Replaying that exact received state through the identical deployed renderer preserves action, dimension, coordinates, status, reason, source and age at both 400 and 700 tokens (399/695 used). This replay confirms context rendering, rather than claiming to inspect the model's internal beliefs. Plugin/model/main/viewer health all returned HTTP 200; the model is loaded, the game is online, and health/food are 20/20. Observed position has risen from Y34 to Y46; ore collection and complete recovery of the preparation loop are not established.
